      "id": 1,
      "text": "Río Grande was founded July 16, 1840 by Desiderio and Quilimaco Escobar with Governor Miguel López's approval.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%ADo_Grande%2C_Puerto_Rico"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Río Grande takes its name from the Río Grande river where it meets the Río Espíritu Santo.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%ADo_Grande%2C_Puerto_Rico"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A large portion of El Yunque National Forest, including its peak, lies within Río Grande’s borders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%ADo_Grande%2C_Puerto_Rico"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "El Yunque’s highest point, El Toro, rises 3,474 feet (1,070 m) and sits inside Río Grande.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%ADo_Grande%2C_Puerto_Rico"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Río Grande hosts Coco Beach, one of Puerto Rico’s most secluded stretches of shoreline.",
